    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "BUSINESS\nLunch and Dinner\nAuckland to Singapore",
      "2007086102",
      "Summer is upon us in New Zealand. When I create a new recipe,\nI love to bring in fresh natural flavours using seasonal produce.\nThis provides a unique taste experience, texture and nutritional\nbalance to the dish. There is nothing better than enjoying the\nsweet juiciness of a ripe summer tomato. They are terrific roasted,\ntheir flavour is intensified with long slow cooking, served with lemon\ncaramelised snapper they're superb. New Zealand kelp is a type of\nseaweed that once dried, has a lovely fresh salty flavour and makes\na fantastic seasoning. The menu at Vinnies is my canvas on which\nto paint and create dishes using only the freshest produce.\nI take my ideas and develop them into dishes to enhance your dining\nexperience on Air New Zealand - I hope you enjoy your meal.\nGEOFF SCOTT.\nOWNER AND CHEF, VINNIES RESTAURANT, HERNE BAY, AUCKLAND\nLunch Auckland to Singapore\nSTARTER\nSugar cured tuna with chilli kelp seasoning,\npapaya and witloof salad, coriander crème fraîche\nMAIN COURSE\nLemon caramelised snapper, gourmet potatoes,\ntomato and rocket salad with vanilla saffron aioli\nSpicy lamb korma curry with turmeric\nbasmati rice, peas and crispy shallots\nChar sui duck dumplings with water chestnuts,\nchar sui\nsauce and fresh minted salad\nDESSERT\nRed wine pear frangipane\nwith pohutukawa honey cream\nGourmet ice cream dessert of blackcurrant\nand blackberry and peach and mango ice cream\nFRUIT\nA selection of seasonal fruit\nBEVERAGES\nFreshly brewed or decaffeinated coffee,\ntea, herbal tea and hot chocolate\nDinner Auckland to Singapore\nSTARTER\nBlack tiger prawns, roasted pear, rocket\nand walnut salad with lemon olive oil dressing\nMAIN COURSE\nMustard and macadamia nut eye fillet of beef\nwith thyme infused mushroom cream\nSage and fig confit of chicken thigh, parsnip puree,\nmanuka glazed bok choy and herb chicken jus\nSalmon and snapper hotpot with New Zealand\nwasabi udon noodles and broccolini\nDESSERT\nWhite and dark chocolate mousse\nLime and coconut cake\nwith pineapple and rosemary crème fraîche\nCHEESE\nA selection of fine New Zealand cheese\nFRUIT\nA selection of seasonal fruit\nBEVERAGES\nFreshly brewed or decaffeinated coffee,\ntea, herbal tea and hot chocolate"
    ],
